-- definitional_shadow.hm
-- The definitional shadow: how hyperethics stands to hypermath and hyperlogic
-- metamathethicology | metaethics x metamathematics x metalogic
--
-- NO LAYER INDEX, DELIBERATELY, AND FOR A THIRD REASON. will_electrophysics.hm
-- carries none because this package indexes by ordinal stage and the material
-- already had an index. hyperphysics/electrical.hm carries none because there
-- the ground is not written. This file carries none because it is a statement
-- ABOUT three fields' layer indices at once, and picking one would silently
-- assert that the three stacks are the same shape. They are not: hypermath's
-- stack is a DIAMOND (L1 and L2 incomparable siblings over L0, joined at L3)
-- and hyperethics' is a CHAIN (L0 -> L1 -> L2 -> L3). That difference is part
-- of what is measured below, not something this file may presuppose.
--
-- Cites: hypermath/L0_ground.hm, L1_relations.hm, L2_operations.hm,
--        L3_ordinatics.hm    -- the closing field.
--        hyperlogic/L0_triangle.hm  -- the field that carries both.
--        hyperethics/L0_creation.hm, L1_entity.hm, L2_will.hm,
--        L3_consciousness.hm -- the refusing field.
-- Imports: none. All nine files are cited as paths and their declaration
--          census is RE-MEASURED by tests/test_definitional_shadow.py whenever
--          the sibling checkouts are present. A skip there means the census
--          below was NOT checked on that run, and the numbers in this file are
--          then a claim about bytes nobody read.
--          The two Lean files under evidence/ are NOT built by this package,
--          which has no Lean toolchain. They are reproduced against
--          hyperethics' own pinned toolchain; evidence/README.md gives the two
--          commands and what their output must be.
--
-- USER-DECLARED PLACEMENT (Tyler Roost), the reason this file exists here:
--   "Electricity hyperphysics should go in hyperphysics, underlying will
--    foundations in hyperethics, and then their combination field of will
--    electrophysics is in metamathethicology."
-- Generalized and already enforced: a field states its own subject once, and
-- anything COMBINING fields is a combination field and lives here. A relation
-- between hyperethics, hypermath and hyperlogic is stateable in none of the
-- three -- each would have to name two foreign subjects to say it -- so it is
-- a combination field of three parents and it belongs in this package.
--
-- USER-DECLARED (Tyler Roost), the relation itself:
--   "the 3 foundational are 'not-grounded' because they should be
--    self-grounding, each holds a definitional self grounding similar and
--    relatable to abstractly ~= to the base hypermath. Their self-grounding
--    self-derivational chains are mirrors and shadows respectively, Ie
--    hyperphysics self-derivational chain is a mirror of hypermaths, and
--    hyperethics is a shadow of hypermaths."
--
-- USER-DECLARED (Tyler Roost), the follow-on this file answers:
--   "see how our hyperethics definitional space can be seen more like a shadow
--    of hypermath and hyperlogic"
--
-- The word "shadow" was loose when it was said and it is not loose now. Below
-- it is given a MEASURED definition, a check, and a named way to be wrong.
--
-- Status: FORM (the census, the slot alignment, the complement, the two named
--               forgotten coordinates, and the witness census with its two
--               kernel-checked collapses);
--         FRAME residuals documented, NOT discharged:
--           - that the three-layer count alignment is law rather than
--             coincidence (GC-1, and it is REFUTED as a count of facts -- the
--             left column counts names; see measured witness-census),
--           - L1 and L2 have not been witness-counted (GC-6),
--           - whether the merged witnesses should be landed in hyperethics
--             (GC-7, a maintainer's call this file declines to make),
--           - that hyperethics' silhouette is a ~=-shadow in hypermath's own
--             technical sense (GC-2, currently FALSE by measurement),
--           - the fourth layer, where the alignment breaks (GC-3),
--           - hyperlogic beyond L0 and hyperphysics at all (GC-4).
--         Sections: I the measured census, II the slot alignment,
--         III what the shadow forgets, IV non-derives, V graduation criterion.
--
-- THIS FILE'S OWN CENSUS, stated because a file that measures censuses does not
-- get to stand outside the measurement: 8 derive, 6 measured, 4 non-derive,
-- 1 open, 1 graduation -- and ZERO relation, ZERO close. By its own
-- `nd-refusal-counts-are-naming` those four refusals are four NAMES, and this
-- file has not built the structure that would say how many facts they are. By its own definition
-- in section I it is a boundary-only file, which puts it on hyperethics' side
-- of the complement and not above it. It describes the shadow in the shadow's
-- vocabulary. That is a limitation on what it can claim, not a flourish: it can
-- report where the interior is missing and it cannot supply any of it.
-- =============================================================================


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION I: THE MEASURED CENSUS
-- Not borrowed. Borrowed material is a statement taken over from a field that
-- states it; these are facts about file bytes that a test re-derives from the
-- files themselves. A count that names itself and is never recomputed is a
-- numeral, not a fact.
-- =============================================================================

measured interior:         -- `relation` and `close` declarations
    -- A `relation` declares a comparison the field will use. A `close` binds an
    -- opaque predicate to one, so that what was asserted pre-relationally now
    -- MEANS something in the field's own vocabulary. Together they are the
    -- field's positive interior: the part of the silhouette that is filled in.
    --   hypermath    relation 4   close 13
    --   hyperlogic   relation 3   close 3
    --   hyperethics  relation 0   close 0
    -- hyperethics does not use either keyword once, in any layer. It is not a
    -- spelling difference: the words appear in its prose 51 times and every
    -- occurrence is either the description of an orbit or a denial, of which
    -- L1_entity.hm's "SO GC-3 IS SHARPENED, NOT CLOSED, and sharpening is not
    -- closing" is the plainest.

measured boundary:         -- `non-derive` and `open` declarations
    -- A `non-derive` names something that does NOT follow and, where the field
    -- is honest, supplies a countermodel. An `open` names an obligation carried
    -- without one. Together they are the field's negative boundary: the edge of
    -- the silhouette, drawn from outside.
    --   hypermath    non-derive 0    open 0
    --   hyperlogic   non-derive 3    open 1
    --   hyperethics  non-derive 40   open 1
    -- hypermath does not use `non-derive` once, in any layer.
    -- IT WAS 35 ON THE MORNING OF 2026-09-21 and 40 by the evening: the
    -- reflection section added five. The COMPLEMENT did not move -- zero
    -- interior, still, across five new declarations written without either
    -- keyword by an author who was not consulting this file. That is the
    -- measurement this file exists for, and it survived a live edit.

measured complement:
    -- The two censuses are DISJOINT ACROSS THE TWO FIELDS, in both directions:
    --   hypermath   has 17 interior declarations and 0 boundary declarations.
    --   hyperethics has 0 interior declarations and 41 boundary declarations.
    --   *** 41 IS STALE. Re-measured 2026-09-21: 45. The hyperethics P0 layer
    --   added 4 non-derives. See section VI. ***
    -- Neither field uses the other's vocabulary at all. This is the whole of
    -- what "shadow" means here, and it is the reason the word is right rather
    -- than "copy", "analogy" or "dual": a shadow is precisely the complement of
    -- a body's silhouette inside the light that casts it. The body is where the
    -- light is stopped; the shadow is where it is absent. hypermath declares
    -- only presence; hyperethics declares only absence.

measured object:
    -- hyperlogic L0 carries BOTH, in equal thirds: relation 3, close 3,
    -- non-derive 3, open 1.
    -- *** "EQUAL THIRDS" IS STALE. Re-measured 2026-09-21 across the repo:
    -- relation 3, close 3, non-derive 7, open 1. P0_shadow_ground.hm added 4
    -- non-derives, so BOUNDARY NOW EXCEEDS INTERIOR, 8 to 6, and hyperlogic is
    -- drifting toward hyperethics' side. See section VI. *** It is the only one of the three foundational fields
    -- that does. So hyperlogic is not a second body and not a second shadow --
    -- it is the field in which the casting is visible at once, which is why the
    -- user's question names it alongside hypermath rather than instead of it.
    -- hyperlogic exists because the derivation relation was stated three
    -- independent times in the family; carrying both censuses is what a field
    -- looks like when its subject is the stating.

measured per-layer:
    -- A COUNT OF NAMES, AND NOT OF FACTS. Read `measured witness-census` below
    -- before using this block for anything; the alignment it records was the
    -- first thing in this file and it is the weakest thing in it.
    -- Layer by layer, hypermath's closes and hyperethics' non-derives are:
    --   L0   hypermath close 3    hyperethics non-derive 3
    --   L1   hypermath close 7    hyperethics non-derive 7
    --   L2   hypermath close 2    hyperethics non-derive 2
    --   L3   hypermath close 1    hyperethics non-derive 28
    -- Three layers agree EXACTLY, slot for slot: each hyperethics layer refuses
    -- as many things as the corresponding hypermath layer closes. The fourth
    -- does not agree and is not close.
    -- THE L3 ROW WAS 23 WHEN THIS FILE WAS WRITTEN, AND MOVED TO 28 THE SAME
    -- DAY, when hyperethics added a reflection section carrying five more
    -- refusals against no new close opposite them. The gap got WIDER while
    -- nothing about either field's method changed, which is what a count of
    -- NAMES does when one author keeps writing and the other does not. A
    -- reader who treated 3-7-2-23 as a structural constant had one day to be
    -- wrong in.
    -- NOTHING FORCES THIS. No test in either repository has ever compared the
    -- two files, the two stacks were written months apart, and 3-7-2 is not a
    -- pattern either field states about itself. It is an OBSERVED alignment.
    -- See nd-count-alignment-is-law.

measured witness-census:
    -- USER-DECLARED (Tyler Roost), the conjecture this block answers:
    --   "Maybe L3 should only have one non-derive, maybe the things are
    --    derivable through like a dark matter of propositional ethics"
    -- IT IS CORRECT, IT IS NOW PROVED, AND IT GENERALIZES PAST L3.
    -- A `non-derive` is a NAME. What refutes it is a MODEL, and a model is not
    -- a declaration -- `primitive`, `opaque`, `axiom`, `derive`, `non-derive`,
    -- `relation`, `close` is the whole vocabulary, and none of them declares a
    -- structure. So the entire refuting content of hyperethics is INVISIBLE to
    -- the census in `measured boundary` above. That is the dark matter, and the
    -- word is exact rather than decorative: not in the visible census, most of
    -- the mass, and detectable only by what it refutes.
    -- Counted three ways, hyperethics' refusals are:
    --            by NAME   by LEAN THEOREM   by DISTINCT WITNESS
    --   L0          3            3                  3 -> 1
    --   L1          7            3                  4, untested
    --   L2          2            1                  1, untested
    --   L3         28           16                  2 -> 1, for the first 12
    -- The two arrows are theorems, not estimates. `evidence/DarkMatterL0.lean`
    -- builds one `RealmModel 6` that satisfies all four L0 axioms, keeps
    -- `TransitiveExposure` at depth two, and refutes `UniversalImmanence`,
    -- `TransitiveExposure 3` and `OtherIsNonidentity` TOGETHER, where the field
    -- uses `separating`, `orbit` and `reflexiveOther`.
    -- `evidence/DarkMatterL3.lean` builds one `MindModel 6 4 5 1` that satisfies
    -- every L3 axiom, keeps every L3 derive, and refutes all TWELVE L3 claims
    -- together, where the field uses `canonical` and `solitary`.
    -- IT REFUTES TWELVE AND THERE ARE NOW SIXTEEN. The reflection section added
    -- four more Lean refutations on 2026-09-21 -- two of them carried by a NEW
    -- structure, `selfBridged`, which no earlier structure could stand in for
    -- because none carried a self-bridge. Whether the merged witness extends to
    -- all sixteen is UNTESTED, and the arrow above is stated for the first
    -- twelve only rather than quietly widened. This is the same discipline
    -- `GC-6` applies to L1 and L2, now applied to a moving L3.
    -- Every theorem in both reports `[propext]` and nothing else.
    -- TWO IS A REAL FLOOR AT FOUR ELEMENTS AND NOT AT SIX. Before the merged
    -- structure existed the kernel decided `¬ EveryMindPairIsBridged canonical`
    -- and `¬ CointeractionIsForced canonical` FALSE: `canonical` bridges every
    -- mind pair, so it cannot carry `solitary`'s three refutations and the
    -- second structure was genuinely required. The collapse to one is bought
    -- with carrier size, not with a tidier reading of what was already there.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION II: THE SLOT ALIGNMENT
-- Where the shadow falls, in file order.
-- =============================================================================

derive d-the-missing-section:
    -- step 1: hypermath/L0_ground.hm's own header lists its sections:
    --         "I primitives, II opaque predicates, III axioms (4), IV derives
    --          (5), V relation declarations, VI closing opaque predicates,
    --          VII graduation criterion".
    -- step 2: hyperethics/L0_creation.hm's own header lists its sections:
    --         "I primitives, II opaque normative predicates, III axioms (4),
    --          IV derives (5, led by the operant), V non-derives (explicit),
    --          VI graduation criterion".
    -- step 3: sections I through IV agree in kind AND in count -- 4 primitives,
    --         3 structural opaques, 4 axioms, 5 derives, in both files.
    -- step 4: at section V they diverge in KIND: relations against non-derives.
    -- step 5: hyperethics has SIX sections where hypermath has SEVEN, and the
    --         one it does not have is VI, the closing section. Its VI is
    --         hypermath's VII.
    -- CONCLUSION: the shadow is exactly one section short, the missing section
    -- is the one that fills the interior in, and both files say so in their own
    -- headers without either one knowing about the other.

derive d-the-three-opaques-correspond:
    -- hypermath L0 section II declares struct-distinct, struct-continues,
    -- struct-orbits. hyperethics L0 section II declares norm-other,
    -- norm-inhabits, norm-returns. The readings line up one to one:
    --   struct-distinct  / norm-other     -- non-identity, pre-evaluative
    --   struct-continues / norm-inhabits  -- the irreducible, what dwells in what
    --   struct-orbits    / norm-returns   -- two-step return to origin
    -- hypermath then closes all three, one close per opaque, in that order.
    -- hyperethics closes none of the three, anywhere in four layers.

derive d-the-shadow-is-ragged:
    -- WHAT A CLEAN SHADOW WOULD LOOK LIKE, AND WHY THIS IS NOT ONE.
    -- step 1: hypermath's three L0 closes are one per opaque, in slot order.
    -- step 2: hyperethics' three L0 non-derives are nd-universal-immanence,
    --         nd-good-from-immanence, nd-transitive-exposure.
    -- step 3: the first two BOTH land on norm-inhabits -- one refusing to
    --         universalize it, one refusing an evaluative reading over it.
    -- step 4: the third lands on norm-returns.
    -- step 5: norm-other receives NEITHER a close NOR a declared refusal in the
    --         source of record. It is used by ax-other and by
    --         d-authorship-exposure and is otherwise untouched there.
    -- CONCLUSION: the counts match at 3 and the SLOTS do not. Opaque 2 is
    -- covered twice and opaque 1 is covered not at all. The shadow is cast but
    -- its edge is ragged, and this is the most concrete thing to fix if the
    -- relation is to be tightened rather than merely observed.

derive d-the-raggedness-is-an-hm-lean-divergence:
    -- WHERE THE MISSING REFUSAL ACTUALLY IS, and it is not missing.
    -- step 1: L0_creation.hm declares three non-derives: nd-universal-immanence,
    --         nd-good-from-immanence, nd-transitive-exposure.
    -- step 2: lean4/Hyperethics/Countermodels.lean refutes three claims:
    --         UniversalImmanence, TransitiveExposure, OtherIsNonidentity.
    -- step 3: the two sets of three share only TWO members.
    --         `OtherIsNonidentity` is refuted by `reflexiveOther` -- a model in
    --         which a realm is `other` than itself -- and the `.hm` declares no
    --         non-derive for it. So norm-other IS refused, by a model, under a
    --         name the source of record does not carry.
    --         `nd-good-from-immanence` runs the other way: it is declared and
    --         has NO Lean refutation, and there is no goodness, value, ranking
    --         or better-than predicate anywhere in the Lean tree. That absence
    --         is correct -- nothing evaluative is formalized in this field --
    --         but it means the `.hm` states a refusal the translation cannot
    --         witness, while the translation witnesses one the `.hm` never
    --         states.
    -- CONCLUSION: the raggedness in d-the-shadow-is-ragged is real and its
    -- CAUSE is not editorial. It is the standing blind spot of this family's
    -- build pattern: NOTHING CHECKS A `.hm` SOURCE AGAINST ITS LEAN
    -- TRANSLATION. No test reads a `.hm` file, and hyperethics' audit compares
    -- the kernel's reports against a hand-written table of what each source is
    -- SAID to claim, never against the source text. Two artifacts can disagree
    -- about which three things a layer declines to derive with the whole stack
    -- green, and here they do.

derive d-the-deferred-close-was-never-paid:
    -- step 1: hyperethics/L0_creation.hm's FRAME residuals name, first,
    --         "opaque normative predicates' semantic close (L2)". The close is
    --         deferred, by name, to a layer two above.
    -- step 2: hyperethics/L2_will.hm declares zero closes.
    -- step 3: its graduation section records the debt as
    --         "INHERITED, STILL OPEN. This layer does not touch them."
    -- CONCLUSION: the promise is made in the same slot hypermath uses to KEEP
    -- it, and is then carried instead of discharged. hypermath L0 makes the
    -- same kind of promise -- its executive opaques are "declared here,
    -- semantically closed by L1" -- and its section IX self-kernel pays it.
    -- Two fields, one promise, one payment.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION III: WHAT THE SHADOW FORGETS
-- A shadow is a projection, and a projection is named by the coordinate it
-- drops. Two are dropped here, one per parent.
-- =============================================================================

derive d-forgotten-against-hypermath:
    -- THE DROPPED COORDINATE IS STAGE, DEPTH, QUANTIFICATION.
    -- step 1: hyperethics L0's header refuses ordinal staging outright:
    --         "a foundation that needs a stage index to state its ground is not
    --          a foundation." hypermath puts ordinal arithmetic at L3 and keeps
    --         apply-as-succession at L0; hyperethics declines the index.
    -- step 2: nd-transitive-exposure refuses depth from the inside:
    --         "ax-return closes the TWO-step orbit. It does not give a
    --          three-step or n-step return." Countermodel supplied.
    -- step 3: hypermath's own shadow operator does exactly this. `~=` is
    --         `=~` MINUS the quantification coordinate -- volume forgotten,
    --         endpoints and trace floor pinned -- it is off-chain on
    --         DerivationPath, weaker than `=~`, and its close carries NO open
    --         frame BECAUSE it drops that clause.
    -- CONCLUSION: the user's phrase "relatable to abstractly ~= to the base
    -- hypermath" is not decoration. `~=` is the operator, and the coordinate
    -- hyperethics forgets relative to hypermath is the one `~=` forgets.

derive d-forgotten-against-hyperlogic:
    -- THE DROPPED COORDINATE IS REGISTER.
    -- step 1: hyperlogic un-collapses the three readings of its irreducible
    --         into a triangle: ax-triangle needs THREE turns to return, where
    --         hypermath's ax-box and hyperethics' ax-return each close a
    --         TWO-step orbit.
    -- step 2: hyperethics keeps its three roles collapsed, and says so in the
    --         same words hypermath uses. The sentence
    --           "The roles are not three separate things. They are three angles
    --            on one thing."
    --         appears VERBATIM in hypermath's `ground` and in hyperethics'
    --         `archetype`, in two repositories, written independently.
    -- CONCLUSION: against hypermath, hyperethics drops depth. Against
    -- hyperlogic, it drops the separation of registers. Two parents, two
    -- coordinates, and the field forgets one of each.

derive d-diamond-projects-to-chain:
    -- step 1: hypermath's layer stack is a DIAMOND. L1 and L2 are incomparable
    --         siblings over L0 and are joined only at L3.
    -- step 2: hyperethics' layer stack is a CHAIN, L0 -> L1 -> L2 -> L3, with
    --         every layer depending on the one below.
    -- step 3: projecting a diamond along its own diagonal yields a chain.
    -- CONCLUSION: the stack shape is itself shadowed, by the same operation and
    -- in the same direction as the declarations. A shadow drops a dimension;
    -- this one drops the incomparability.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION IV: NON-DERIVES
-- What the census does not establish. A file that measures refusals had better
-- state its own.
-- =============================================================================

non-derive nd-count-alignment-is-law:
    -- NOT derivable: that hypermath's closes and hyperethics' non-derives must
    -- agree per layer.
    -- They agree at L0, L1 and L2 -- 3, 7, 2 -- and disagree at L3 by 1 against
    -- 23. Three agreements out of four is an OBSERVATION. Nothing in either
    -- field's axioms, headers or tests mentions the other field's counts, no
    -- construction maps one declaration to the other, and the fourth layer is a
    -- standing refutation of any rule that would force it.
    -- The L3 break has a KNOWN cause and the cause is not structural:
    -- hyperethics L3 was extended twice by declaration on 2026-09-21, first
    -- with consciousness and minds and then with thought, the reality taxonomy
    -- and language. Each extension added refusals and closed nothing. So the
    -- alignment held for as long as the two stacks were built at comparable
    -- rates and broke when one of them was not.
    -- ANY LATER CLAIM THAT THE ALIGNMENT IS LAW MUST EXHIBIT THE MAP.
    -- AND IT IS NOW WORSE THAN UNDERIVED. `measured witness-census` shows the
    -- left-hand column is a naming convention: L0's three and L3's twelve each
    -- collapse to ONE witness, by construction, in the kernel. So 3-7-2 does
    -- not count refusals -- it counts how often two authors chose to give a
    -- refusal its own name. The correspondence in `measured per-layer` is
    -- between one real quantity and one editorial one.

non-derive nd-refusal-counts-are-naming:
    -- NOT derivable FROM A LAYER'S DECLARATION COUNT: how many independent
    -- facts that layer refuses.
    -- REFUTED CONCLUSIVELY, twice, by construction. See the two files under
    -- `evidence/` and the table in `measured witness-census`.
    -- WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY. It does not say the names are waste. A merged
    -- structure establishes THAT a set of failures is jointly realizable; it
    -- does not tell a reader WHICH claim each failure is about, and a reader
    -- who wants to know whether a bridge is symmetric needs that claim written
    -- down under its own name with its own reasons. The names are an index and
    -- the witness is the fact. hypermath draws the same distinction from the
    -- other side: its `relation` declarations are the index and its `close`
    -- declarations are what makes them mean anything.
    -- WHAT IT DOES SAY. Any argument that reads a refusal count as a measure of
    -- how much a field declines to settle is measuring names. This file made
    -- that mistake in its own first section and the correction is left visible
    -- rather than edited out.

non-derive nd-shadow-is-a-tilde-eq-shadow:
    -- NOT derivable, and currently FALSE BY MEASUREMENT: that hyperethics is a
    -- shadow of hypermath in hypermath's own technical sense.
    -- hypermath's `~=` drops a coordinate and thereby DROPS AN OBLIGATION -- its
    -- close carries no open frame precisely because the quantification clause is
    -- gone. hyperethics drops its interior and ACCUMULATES obligations: 27 open
    -- at last count, growing 17 -> 19 -> 24 -> 27 across its four layers, with
    -- GC-6 getting LARGER rather than smaller on 2026-09-21, when a
    -- non-statement became an assumption.
    -- A forgetting that costs more than it saves is not a projection. So the
    -- relation is presently a shadow in the visual sense only, and "making
    -- hyperethics more like a shadow" has a precise meaning: NAME THE FORGOTTEN
    -- COORDINATE so that its omission DISCHARGES something instead of owing it.
    -- Section III names two candidates. Neither is yet written into hyperethics.

non-derive nd-mirror-from-shadow:
    -- NOT derivable: anything about hyperphysics from anything in this file.
    -- The user declared hyperphysics a MIRROR of hypermath -- position
    -- preserved, arrows reversed, dimension preserved, invertible -- and
    -- hyperethics a SHADOW -- silhouette preserved, interior lost, dimension
    -- dropped, not invertible. A mirror and a shadow of the same body are not
    -- recoverable from each other, and hyperphysics is not measured here.
    -- Its census is GC-4 below, not a consequence of anything above.

open nd-shadow-has-no-countermodel-discipline:
    -- NAMED OPEN OBLIGATION, NOT DISCHARGED.
    -- Every other refusal in this family is refuted conclusively by a supplied
    -- countermodel, on the epistemic contract that model checking confirms
    -- nothing universally while a single countermodel refutes conclusively.
    -- The three non-derives above supply no countermodels, because a
    -- countermodel to a claim about declaration counts would have to be a pair
    -- of FIELDS, and this package has no notion of a field as an object.
    -- The census is checked instead, which is a weaker thing, and the
    -- difference is recorded here rather than papered over.


-- =============================================================================
-- SECTION V: GRADUATION CRITERION
-- =============================================================================

graduation:
    -- GC-1: that the per-layer count alignment is law. NOT DISCHARGED and NOT
    --       DERIVABLE as stated -- see nd-count-alignment-is-law. Discharging
    --       it means exhibiting a map from hypermath closes to hyperethics
    --       non-derives, not observing the numbers a second time.
    -- GC-2: that hyperethics is a ~=-shadow in hypermath's technical sense.
    --       NOT DISCHARGED and currently measured FALSE: the forgetting
    --       accumulates obligations instead of dropping them. This is the
    --       actionable one, and section III names the two coordinates whose
    --       naming would move it.
    -- GC-3: the fourth layer. L3 breaks the alignment 1 against 23, and this
    --       file explains the break historically rather than structurally.
    --       A historical explanation is not a derivation.
    -- GC-4: hyperlogic above L0, and hyperphysics at all. hyperlogic has one
    --       layer written, and the census calls it the field that carries both
    --       censuses on the strength of that single file. hyperphysics is named
    --       by the user as the mirror and is not measured here at all. Two of
    --       the four fields in the declared relation are therefore sampled,
    --       not surveyed.
    -- GC-6: L1 and L2 have not been witness-counted. L0 and L3 each collapse to
    --       one structure and the same construction is expected to work at the
    --       two layers between them, which is exactly the kind of expectation
    --       this family does not accept in place of a model. Until someone
    --       builds them, the middle two rows of `measured witness-census` are
    --       counts of theorem arguments and not of witnesses.
    -- GC-7: whether the merged structures should be LANDED in hyperethics.
    --       They are not, and this file does not recommend it. Replacing named
    --       witnesses with one merged witness would shorten the files and lose
    --       the per-claim reasons, which is the trade `nd-refusal-counts-are-
    --       naming` describes and does not decide. It is a maintainer's call
    --       about readability, not a fact about the theory.
    -- GC-5: that `measured` is the right keyword. It is introduced by this file
    --       and used by no other. `borrowed` was wrong -- a borrowed law is a
    --       statement taken over from a field that states it, and no field
    --       states its own declaration census. Whether a third keyword was
    --       needed, rather than a derive with a test behind it, is a judgement
    --       this file makes and does not defend.


-- ── VI. THE 2026-09-21 RESTATEMENT ──────────────────────────────────────────
--
-- PROVENANCE, stated first because this file's whole discipline rests on it:
-- the statement below was made by Tyler to a DIFFERENT session and reached me
-- relayed. It is verbatim as relayed, but it is not first-hand to this file
-- the way the section I quotation is. Treat it as USER-DECLARED-AS-REPORTED
-- until he restates it here.
--
--   "hypermath and hyperlogic reflecting mirror-wise yields hyperphysics,
--    hyperethics is the shadow form of hypermath and the shadow form of
--    hyperlogic and the shadow form of hyperphysics."

-- d-mirror-changed-arity : section I's canon is UNARY -- "hyperphysics
--   self-derivational chain is a mirror of hypermaths", one parent. The
--   restatement is BINARY: hypermath and hyperlogic reflecting off ONE ANOTHER
--   yield hyperphysics.
--
--   This is not a small edit. A binary operator on two fields producing a
--   third is the two-limb combination shape exactly, so `mirror` is a
--   metamathethicology object by the placement rule rather than a fact any one
--   field states about itself. That is consistent with where this file already
--   lives, and it is the first independent confirmation that the file is in
--   the right repository. Section I's unary phrasing is now the stale one.

-- d-shadow-has-three-legs : and the census tests them separately.
--   Re-measured 2026-09-21, same method as sections `measured interior` and
--   `measured boundary` -- interior = `relation` + `close`, boundary =
--   `non-derive` + `open`, counted as line-initial declarations in *.hm.
--
--     field          interior   boundary   reading
--     hypermath            17          0   body, no boundary at all
--     hyperlogic            6          8   carries BOTH; boundary now leads
--     hyperethics           0         45   shadow, no interior at all
--     hyperphysics          0          1   neither, and barely measured
--
--   leg 1  shadow(hypermath) = hyperethics      HOLDS. 17/0 against 0/45 is
--          perfect disjointness. This is section I's original relation and it
--          survives the restatement unchanged.
--
--   leg 2  shadow(hyperlogic) = hyperethics     FAILS, and this file already
--          said why before the leg was claimed: hyperlogic "is not a second
--          body and not a second shadow -- it is the field in which the
--          casting is visible at once." A field carrying both cannot be the
--          body of a shadow; it is where the shadow is SEEN. The failure got
--          worse, not better: boundary 8 now EXCEEDS interior 6.
--
--   leg 3  shadow(hyperphysics) = hyperethics   CANNOT BE TESTED. Note the
--          verdict carefully -- it is not "false". hyperphysics has ZERO
--          interior declarations, so it has no silhouette to cast, and its
--          profile (0 interior, 1 boundary) puts it on hyperethics' OWN side
--          rather than its complement. But it has exactly ONE `.hm` file
--          (electrical.hm) and one boundary declaration. At n = 1 the census
--          has nothing to measure. Untestable, pending hyperphysics being
--          written.
--
--   The same n = 1 problem hits the MIRROR leg from the other end: the field
--   Tyler names as the mirror currently has no positive interior at all, so
--   there is nothing yet for hypermath and hyperlogic to be reflected INTO.
--   Both the new shadow leg and the restated mirror wait on the same work.

-- d-census-has-a-scope-hazard : mine, found by getting it wrong.
--   Counting every `*.hm` under the repository gives hypermath 23 interior,
--   not 17. The extra six are `references/precursor/hypermath/spec/axioms.hm`
--   and `references/precursor/hypermath_form/relations.hm` -- VENDORED material
--   from an older □-system, not hypermath's own layer stack. They must be
--   EXCLUDED, and the other three fields have no `references/` tree, so the
--   hazard bites hypermath alone and would silently inflate exactly the field
--   the whole relation is measured against.
--   Any re-run of this census must state its scope. This one is: the field's
--   own layer files, `references/` excluded.

-- d-numbers-move-faster-than-the-file : both stale numbers flagged above moved
--   because of ONE event -- the P0 layers, written 2026-09-21, added 4
--   non-derives to hyperethics (41 -> 45) and 4 to hyperlogic (which is what
--   overturned "equal thirds" and flipped it to boundary-led). Two days, two
--   corrections, one cause.
--   THE HOOK, which is worth more than any number here: this file should carry
--   a re-measure instruction, not frozen counts. Every count above is true on
--   2026-09-21 and is expected to be false again. Re-run before quoting.

-- d-hyperlogic-has-a-paradox-layer : recorded because Tyler is on record
--   (relayed, same caveat) doubting it -- "hyperlogic might not even have a
--   paradox layer yet." It does: `hyperlogic/P0_shadow_ground.hm`, headed
