-- nd-ppl-states-are-tylers-operators : do NOT assume PPL's SHADOW_PARADOX and
--   MIRROR_PARADOX are the two operators above under other names. The ARITIES
--   DISAGREE, and that is evidence against identity, not a detail: PPL's pair
--   are dual verdict states one bit apart on the convergence bit, over a
--   single object. Tyler's are operators over FIELDS -- mirror binary, shadow
--   unary. Same two English words, third and fourth senses, and the collision
--   is now catalogued in VOCABULARY_BOUNDARY.md as words 9 and 10.
--   Checking whether they are secretly the same structure is legitimate work.
--   Assuming it is how a fifth sense gets created.

-- CITATION, RESOLVED -- and the two halves live in different repositories,
-- which is the part a later reader needs.
--   The DECLARATION `nd-p0-shadows-hypermath` is in
--   `hyperlogic/P0_shadow_ground.hm`, which is UNTRACKED in hyperlogic. Verified
--   by reading the working tree.
--   The COMMIT 719585b is in `meta-morphoscripted-origination` -- "Record PPL's
--   standing per Tyler, the hyperlogic corroboration, and reopen shadow/mirror",
--   2026-09-21, touching PLACEMENT.md, and UNPUSHED. It RECORDS the observation;
--   it does not contain the declaration.
--   So following the commit id will not show you the non-derive, and the file
--   that holds the non-derive is in no commit at all. Both halves are one
--   deletion away from each other.
--
-- I first wrote here that 719585b "exists in none of" five repositories. It
-- exists in the sixth, the one I did not search. The claim was universal; the
-- search was bounded and the bound went unstated. Same shape as the census
